WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.000
- [Mark] All right, Glow.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.833
- Yeah.

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:23.070
- [Mark] Glow, Where
are you from originally?

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:23.990
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.490
- [Glow] California?

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.010
- [Mark] What part?

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:27.950
- [Glow] Bakersfield.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:28.783
- [Mark] Bakersfield.

00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:29.616
- [Glow] Yeah.

00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:30.449
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:31.540
You grew up with both of your parents.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.950
You were raised by them?
- No, my mother.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.170
My father took off

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.386
and I didn't get raised
with him, just my mother.

00:00:38.386 --> 00:00:40.680
- [Mark] Did you ever
spend time with your dad?

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.853
- I called him one time when I was 17.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:44.990
It was during the holidays

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.950
and he told me that he was
spending Christmas and New Year's

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.040
with his family and had
to get back to them.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:49.873
So when I hung up,

00:00:49.873 --> 00:00:51.240
I figured 17 years without him,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.450
17 more won't hurt.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.198
So I haven't talked to him since.

00:00:54.198 --> 00:00:55.730
- [Mark] Okay.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:56.880
How was your childhood?

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.003
- Wonderful.

00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:01.730
My mother was the homemaker

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.180
and Sunday school teacher
all wrapped in one.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.060
She made everything
even down to the bread,

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.820
baked bread till I was about 10 years old

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.200
and I was very sick in school.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.790
So she would make homemade food

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.340
for lunches and stuff like that.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.450
She's a good mom.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.283
- [Mark] That's great.

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:18.223
And what kind of kid
were you in high school?

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.400
- I didn't do well in school.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.863
I was very shy.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.600
Not social, so I didn't
do too well in school

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.720
but I made it to the 11th grade

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.360
and then I went to work instead
of finishing school at home.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.810
That was better financially
for me and my mother.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.523
- [Mark] And what age were
you when you left home?

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:43.980
- It was late bloomer.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:44.873
I was 20.

00:01:48.046 --> 00:01:49.746
- [Mark] And where'd you go?

00:01:49.746 --> 00:01:51.963
- LA for a while.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.170
- [Mark] Do you have kids?

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.023
- I have one son.

00:01:57.066 --> 00:01:57.899
- [Mark] And you raised him?

00:01:57.899 --> 00:01:59.470
- I did, yeah.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.790
Just like me, he looks just like me.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:02.623
He's a good kid.

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:04.890
He finished school, great grades.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:05.920
Bring into the service,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.220
no pregnancies, no children,

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.243
no marriages, no drugs.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.425
A good kid.

00:02:11.425 --> 00:02:12.880
I did okay.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.780
- [Mark] You did a good job.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.420
- Yeah.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.940
- [Mark] And so now
you're living on Skid Row?

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.773
- I am.

00:02:18.773 --> 00:02:20.193
- [Mark] How'd you end up down here?

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.190
- Well, I had been in Lancaster

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.810
and I was staying with a guy

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.890
and he decided to put
me up against the wall

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.253
and then hit me and pushed me out the car.

00:02:29.253 --> 00:02:30.270
- [Mark] Hit you what?

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.103
- Pardon?

00:02:31.103 --> 00:02:31.936
- [Mark] Hit you how?

00:02:31.936 --> 00:02:33.570
- He hit me when I was in the car

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.860
then leaned over and grabbed the door

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.233
and pushed me, took off.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.000
I figured Lancaster wasn't gonna get me.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.042
If anything was gonna get me

00:02:44.042 --> 00:02:45.420
and take me out of somewhere,

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.580
I figured it might as well be LA.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.620
So I came here with a couple of kids,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.453
a couple of young kids.

00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:51.595
I was like their aunt for a while.

00:02:51.595 --> 00:02:55.050
And they got into drugs real
heavy and needles and stuff

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.090
and I can't go that direction
'cause my body won't let me.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.763
So they split and ended
up staying and here I am.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.570
- [Mark] And are drugs
a part of your life?

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.830
- I do crack on occasion.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.970
My body won't let me get
addicted to anything.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.560
My body shuts down.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.400
I'm very unhealthy on the inside.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.510
There's a lot going on.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.620
So the outside is kind of a fool,

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.410
but hey, if it works,
then that works, I guess.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.510
- [Mark] So you use crack sometimes?

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.343
- I use crack.

00:03:23.343 --> 00:03:26.870
I use marijuana on a religious basis.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.260
Everything makes me feel better.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.520
It helps me to eat,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.580
comes on all the stuff I'm
supposed to take medication for.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.560
So that's probably my main vice

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.180
and I smoke cigarettes

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.130
and I drink when I can.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.243
Like I said, my body is the judge on that.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.940
- [Mark] And how are
you surviving out here?

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.630
What do you do for money or-

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.935
- I'm on disability.

00:03:45.935 --> 00:03:48.170
- [Mark] Disability.
- I'm disabled, yes.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.780
So I have that kind of income

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.250
and I'm looking for an RV
type situation right now

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.890
and within the next month

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.530
to three months, should have an RV

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.170
and to be at least off the street

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.920
someplace where someone can't
say, "You gotta get out."

00:04:02.783 --> 00:04:04.920
- [Mark] Yeah, that'd be
on the streets for a fact.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:05.783
- Not for me.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:07.460
It's rough.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:08.680
The roughness, it's not for me.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.513
It's what it is.

00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:11.030
- [Mark] How many years
have you been on Skid Row?

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.470
- Oh, I have been on Skid Row

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.850
for three months, four months.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:15.683
- [Mark] Oh, that's it?

00:04:15.683 --> 00:04:16.516
- Yeah.

00:04:16.516 --> 00:04:17.349
- [Mark] So you're brand new here?

00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:18.182
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:04:18.182 --> 00:04:19.410
I still get lost when I get turned around

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.833
wet paper sex syndrome.

00:04:20.833 --> 00:04:22.232
- [Mark] Welcome to the shit hole?

00:04:22.232 --> 00:04:23.065
- Pardon?

00:04:23.065 --> 00:04:23.898
- [Mark] Welcome to the shit hole.

00:04:23.898 --> 00:04:26.653
- Oh thank you, glad to be here. (laughs)

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.087
- [Mark] The worst place
on earth or whatever

00:04:30.087 --> 00:04:31.990
- But what better place to start over

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.360
and prove that I can survive?

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.090
Throw it at me, let's go.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:36.923
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.285
So how was your childhood?

00:04:41.285 --> 00:04:43.370
- Oh, my childhood?

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.860
Well, my younger years was great.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:45.693
It was really good.

00:04:45.693 --> 00:04:46.990
My mom took care of everything.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.023
She was awesome.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.480
The only kind of untypical

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.063
I went through 12 stepdads.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.204
The longest one was 10 years.

00:04:59.204 --> 00:05:00.930
- [Mark] You had 12 stepfathers?

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:01.763
- Yes.

00:05:01.763 --> 00:05:03.360
- [Mark] You're mom
married how many times?

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.550
- 12 and according to her,

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.120
all of them should have been my father.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.600
So it was kind of hard to understand

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.550
how men were supposed to be

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.350
because there were so many different

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.620
and it got to the point

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.400
where the only thing I really learned

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.440
was when things got bad, when you get hit,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.083
when you get hurt, pack up and bail.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.590
And that's one of the few things

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.840
I've been really good at.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.020
My third stepfather,

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.923
the one that was the
10 years had raised me.

00:05:41.791 --> 00:05:45.113
And when they split, I went
to live with him for a while.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.653
And for whatever reasons,

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.223
he didn't look at me
as a daughter anymore.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.830
It was confusing

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.730
but I didn't talk to anybody about it.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.423
I'm just not the type to talk.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.030
I had three more that
had done the same thing.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.280
My mother was not aware of it.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.313
I didn't tell her.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.473
So when the last father happened,

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.000
my mother and I,

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.070
we were visiting

00:06:18.059 --> 00:06:20.980
somewhere in LA, I don't
remember at the moment.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.440
And we were at a hotel.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.120
She was a long haul
truck driver at the time.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.700
And then her husband who wasn't there,

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.840
I was visiting her

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.730
